# Ignore personal CV documents.
#
# NOTE THE TRAILING GLOB. This rule used to read `Herman CV.*`, which matches
# `Herman CV.md` and nothing else — `Herman CV_EdUHK.md` and `Herman CV_new.md`
# have an underscore where that pattern wants a dot, so they were tracked and
# public from 2025-12-14 until 2026-07-29 carrying a home address and phone
# number. The comment above stated the intent; the pattern implemented it for one
# file. Anything named `Herman CV<anything>` is now ignored by default.
Herman CV*
# ...except these two, which are deliberately published as part of the CV site and
# carry no contact details. Adding a new variant here is a decision, not an accident.
!Herman CV_EdUHK.md
!Herman CV_new.md

# Ignore product requirement documents
PRD/
IT Examples/

# Node / tooling (if introduced later)
node_modules/
.DS_Store
